# Echo React Image Template Guidelines

## Overview
Echo Image is a React (Vite) application for AI-powered image generation using Echo's user-pays infrastructure. It uses `@merit-systems/echo-react-sdk`.

## Project Structure
- `src/main.tsx` — App entry point with EchoProvider
- `src/App.tsx` — Main app component with image generation UI

## EchoProvider Setup
```typescript
import { EchoProvider } from '@merit-systems/echo-react-sdk';

createRoot(document.getElementById('root')!).render(
  <StrictMode>
    <EchoProvider config={{ appId: import.meta.env.VITE_ECHO_APP_ID! }}>
      <App />
    </EchoProvider>
  </StrictMode>
);
```

## Echo UI Components
```typescript
import { EchoTokens } from '@merit-systems/echo-react-sdk';

function App() {
  return (
    <>
      <EchoTokens />
      {/* Image generation UI */}
    </>
  );
}
```

## Key Patterns
- Use `import.meta.env.VITE_ECHO_APP_ID` for Vite environment variables
- `EchoTokens` handles auth, balance display, and top-up
- Echo manages billing for image generation API calls

## Environment Variables
- `VITE_ECHO_APP_ID` — App ID from the Echo dashboard

## Anti-Patterns (DO NOT)
- ❌ Do NOT use `process.env` — use `import.meta.env` (Vite)
- ❌ Do NOT import AI SDKs directly — Echo handles provider access
- ❌ Do NOT build custom payment flows — use `EchoTokens`
- ❌ Do NOT render Echo components outside `EchoProvider`
